hadiths[6]{hadithnumber,text}:
"15677","Ismail ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Ziyad ibn Mikhraq narrated to us, from Muawiyah ibn Qurrah, from his father, that a man said: O Messenger of Allah, I slaughter a sheep and I pity it, or he said: I pity a sheep to slaughter it. So he said: And a sheep, if you pity it, Allah will pity you."
"15678","Waki narrated to us, from Shubah, from Muawiyah ibn Qurrah, from his father, he said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, wiped over my head."
"15679","Waki narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Muawiyah ibn Qurrah, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Fasting three days of every month is the fasting of a lifetime and its breaking."
"15680","Waki narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Muawiyah ibn Qurrah, from his father, that a man used to come to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, with a son of his. So the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to him: Do you love him. So he said: O Messenger of Allah, may Allah love you as I love him. So the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, missed him, and said to me: What happened to the son of So-and-so. They said: O Messenger of Allah, he died. So the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to his father: Do you not love that you come to no gate among the gates of Paradise except you find him waiting for you. The man said: O Messenger of Allah, is it for him specially or for all of us. He said: Rather for all of you."
"15681","Yazid informed us, Shubah informed us, from Muawiyah ibn Qurrah, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When the people of Sham become corrupt there is no good in you. There will remain people among my nation victorious, not caring who forsakes them until the Hour comes."
"15682","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Shubah, he said: Muawiyah ibn Qurrah narrated to me, from his father, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: When the people of Sham become corrupt there is no good in you. There will remain a group among my nation victorious, those who forsake them will not harm them until the Hour comes."
